#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kiwi-server-gui — edit a fleet file and build its install media.

The window is a fleet on the left (Defaults, then one row per host) and a
form on the right. The form comes from two things: the base fields every host
has (target, role, admin, network, disk, updates) and the settings schema the
selected role publishes through `kiwi-server roles --porcelain` — so a new
role dropped into roles/ gets its form without any change here.

Everything that generates or builds goes through the CLI (`kiwi-server
render` / `build`), streamed into the log pane. The GUI edits YAML and reads
the CLI's --porcelain JSON; it is not a second implementation of anything.
Comments in a fleet file are not kept when the GUI saves it.
"""
